<title>USA: U.S. chain store sales up 0.1 pct -- BTM/Schroders.</title>
<headline>U.S. chain store sales up 0.1 pct -- BTM/Schroders.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. chain store sales rose 0.1 percent in the week ended July 5 from the prior week, according to the seasonally adjusted BTM/Schroders weekly chain store sales index.</p>
<p>Sales for the week were up 3.0 percent on a year-over-year basis, while the month-to-date index slipped 0.2 percent from the prior month.</p>
<p>&quot;A few retailers are experiencing some inventory overhang, prompting some increased markdowns, though most suggest that inventories are well-managed and under control,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
